<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria M1 rises 7.43 pct, M2 up 3.60 pct in week.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria M1 rises 7.43 pct, M2 up 3.60 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian M1 money supply rose to 752.9 billion levs on May 23 from 700.8 billion levs a week earlier and M2 increased to 3,394.4 billion levs from 3,276.6 billion levs, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Total broad money rose 3.10 percent to 3,575.9 billion levs in the week to May 23.</p>
<p>Conversion of dollar-denominated deposits into levs was made at the central bank fixings of 1,566.8 levs per dollar for May 23, 1,511.4 for May 16 and 1,467.8 for April 25.</p>
